<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL RAISES DIESEL PRICE FROM MONDAY.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL RAISES DIESEL PRICE FROM MONDAY.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Friday it will raise its retail price for diesel in the Netherlands by 1.2 cents per litre with effect from September 2.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, Shell said.</p>
<p>From Monday the price of diesel at Shell's self-service stations goes up to 1.432 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>The prices of unleaded gasolines and of premium gasoline with lead substitute remain unchanged.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
